WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.007
Ratio scales have equal differences and a meaningful zero.

00:00:04.007 --> 00:00:06.782
Zero visits means no visits occurred.

00:00:06.782 --> 00:00:10.292
Zero elapsed seconds means no time elapsed.

00:00:10.292 --> 00:00:15.517
Because the zero point represents absence, ratio statements can be meaningful.

00:00:15.517 --> 00:00:18.347
Four visits can be twice two visits.

00:00:18.347 --> 00:00:21.932
Ratio variables support a wide range of arithmetic, although distribution, units,

00:00:21.932 --> 00:00:24.952
and context still affect which summaries are useful.

00:00:24.952 --> 00:00:33.182
The easiest way to classify a variable is to ask what statements are meaningful in the real world.

00:00:33.182 --> 00:00:38.217
Can values only be different, can they be ordered, are differences meaningful, and does zero mean absence?

00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:43.882
Those questions are more reliable than looking at whether the software stores the column as an integer or

00:00:43.882 --> 00:00:46.590
floating-point number.
